WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
On I go, searching for...

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
The past that was stolen from me

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Wandering on through...

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
This city, so strange to see

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Choked by the scent of flames that seems to...

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Cling to me

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Didn't we both say our goodbyes...

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
And go our separate ways?

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
When you see the face of hell...

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
It will squeeze your heart dry

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Fighting on seems so pointless now

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
If this must be my fate...

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Then I'll make my mind up now

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
So, please, won't you just leave me be...

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Another day

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Oh, will tomorrow hold something new to see?

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:40.790
Gilgamesh and Balarant.

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:43.420
For a hundred years now,

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:46.580
these two star systems have been locked in a war
whose cause was long-forgotten.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:50.710
At first, they managed to contain the hostilities.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.130
But, by the time I joined up, the front had expanded...

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:59.710
and the 200 worlds belonging to those two systems
had been caught in the flames of war.

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:03.710
I fought.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.040
At first, I fought sincerely to defend
my homeworld of Melkia.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:14.630
But the war just dragged on and on
with no end in sight...

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:18.380
I'm so tired now.

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:22.080
Everyone is so tired.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:30.330
WAR'S END

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:50.080
Captain Rochina, do you read? This is Karmeny.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.830
I read you, General. Rochina here.

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.500
Are the peace negotiations wrapped up?

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:58.290
Idiot! You think this war can be ended that easily?

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:01.830
Pardon me, Sir. There are rumors flying around about it.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:06.500
General Battentain wants to speak with you. Hang on.

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:10.880
This is Battentain.
Are you familiar with the warship Teltain?

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.380
Yes, Sir. It's based out of planet Berabos, isn't it?

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:16.710
Somebody has hijacked it. I want it found at once!

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:20.290
But I thought the Teltain
was about to be decommissioned.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:21.500
Surely it's not that important...

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:24.210
The ship isn't important? Where it's headed is!

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:28.080
The beacon shows it was on course for LX-2045.

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:32.130
They're finally onto us.

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:35.420
We'll be long gone before they ever get here.

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:40.790
Gentlemen! Get ready! We're almost at the target point.

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:06.040
Oriya! Conin! Are you ready?

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:07.460
Ready and waiting, Sir!

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:09.080
Any problems with the assault team?

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:11.540
No, Sir. We'll do one last check.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.790
And double check the mission disk.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.290
Mission disk checks out.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:20.380
What about the new guy?

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:21.170
Chirico, Sir?

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:24.920
They bumped him in here from Special Forces
without any warning.

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:27.170
We only brought him along to avoid suspicion.

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:30.460
He doesn't know anything. Keep an eye on him.

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:32.380
If he starts to suspect, we'll take care of it.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:33.580
Don't worry, Sir.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.000
All right, get going!

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:41.790
They're friendlies? Sir, we're fighting our own guys?

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:44.960
I'll explain later! Shut up and fight!

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:02.250
We'll split up.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:04.920
All units up to six, with me! The rest, go with Conin!

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:40.710
They're our guys!

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:42.380
Our guys...

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:04.670
Where's Smir?

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:07.540
He got fragged in an EM barrier.

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:08.540
Did you cut the power?

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:10.080
We just did. It's cut!

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:14.670
Chirico... good work!

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:17.630
There're still a few of them left.
Take up a guard position here.

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:20.130
The rest of you, with me!

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:23.080
Lieutenant! Tell me what we're here for!

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:25.040
I'll tell you later!

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:27.290
Why are we attacking our own forces?

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.500
Tell me! Tell me the reason!

00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:35.500
Did you hear me or not?!

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:36.920
But, Sir...!

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:38.380
Do not move from this spot!

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:39.380
That's an order!

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:40.880
L-Lieutenant!

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:43.420
All right, let's go!

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:05.750
Jackpot!

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:07.380
All right!

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:15.040
We just have to find the main item.

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:18.630
It's somewhere close, and it won't be easy to find.

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:21.250
Lieutenant, tell me what this mission's about!

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:24.460
Chirico, shut up or I'll see you in a court martial!

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:25.420
Lieutenant!

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:27.710
Men, switch off Chirico's frequency!

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:28.960
We can't afford all this noise!

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:30.790
Lieutenant! Lieutenant!

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:47.790
What... What is this?

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:54.460
Chirico! What are you doing in there? What's happened?

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:56.880
This... I've found something strange, Sir!

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:58.130
Something strange?

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:02.500
That's what we've been looking for!

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:04.380
Don't worry about it. We'll take it from here.

00:12:04.630 --> 00:12:05.670
Yes, Sir.

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:28.670
Chirico!

00:12:28.670 --> 00:12:29.500
Sir?

00:12:30.130 --> 00:12:32.830
Go check if the mothership's in sight yet.

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:34.460
I want to get this stuff transferred over there.

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:36.210
Yes, Sir.

00:12:44.420 --> 00:12:47.830
They all know what it is. Why keep me in the dark?

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:56.250
And that's a decommissioned ship.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.750
Something stinks about this whole operation!

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:19.380
Excellent. Right, prepare to pull out!

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:53.670
This is the warship Bauntaunt. Come in.

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:56.130
Repeat, this is the warship Bauntaunt.

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:58.790
Do you read? If you can, respond at once!

00:14:14.210 --> 00:14:16.130
Sorry to have awakened you so rudely...

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:17.880
but could you please answer a few questions?

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:20.000
Where... Where am I?

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:23.880
I ask the questions here. Let's start with your name.

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:26.750
Chirico. Chirico Cuvie.

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:28.250
Date of birth?

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:32.290
7 July. Year 2326 of the Gilgamesh calendar.

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:34.540
That'd make you 18. Assignment?

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:37.540
Gilgamesh forces, 24th Melkian front.

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:40.330
2045th Armored Trooper Corps.

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:43.830
What were you doing back there?

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:46.170
Carrying out our mission.

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:47.000
Whose mission?

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:48.080
They wouldn't tell me.

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:49.880
Who were your commanders?

00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:52.790
Oriya... and Conin. I don't know who else!

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:55.960
Who blew up asteroid base Lido?

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:57.420
I don't know.

00:14:57.420 --> 00:14:58.750
Where did they take the Prototype?

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:01.080
Prototype? What do you mean?

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:03.580
There was a container there, like a coffin, right?

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:05.080
That thing...

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:08.000
Did you see what was inside?

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:08.920
Inside?

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:13.000
No, I didn't.

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:15.460
You're lying. Where did you take the Prototype?

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:18.420
I don't know! I don't know where it is!

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:19.670
Quit playing dumb!

00:15:19.670 --> 00:15:21.460
My team turned on me!

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:22.960
I don't know what happened after...

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:31.210
Well?

00:15:31.210 --> 00:15:32.670
He's fainted!

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:35.380
Looks like the shock was too powerful.

00:15:36.630 --> 00:15:39.380
I never would have thought it'd be our own people.

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:43.460
What do you think, Captain Rochina?

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:47.960
General Battentain, this man is the only clue we have.

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:51.000
We have to get what we need out of him.

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:53.670
As if we didn't have enough problems.

00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:56.830
We'd better get the treaty with Balarant finalized soon.

00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:58.830
Before the secret gets out.

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:02.000
Yes, Sir. I'll return to Melkia at once.

00:16:02.710 --> 00:16:04.790
And I'll take my time in dealing with him.

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:26.040
So, how does it feel to return to your homeworld?

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:29.210
Melkia... Is it really bad down there?

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:32.790
Very. Three-quarters of the population is dead.

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:35.960
I suppose one more or less really wouldn't matter much.

00:17:23.750 --> 00:17:24.880
Well?

00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:28.080
Sir, he's taken three hours of neuro shocks so far.

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:29.960
An unusually stubborn case.

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:31.960
Chirico! Just tell us the truth!

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:33.000
Where is the Prototype?

00:17:33.670 --> 00:17:35.960
I can't tell you what I don't know!

00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:37.630
Increase the power.

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:40.040
No! He'll never survive!

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:44.250
Dr. Fuusen, you don't seem to appreciate
how serious this is.

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:45.000
But...!

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:45.420
Do it!

00:17:56.960 --> 00:17:57.790
What's wrong?

00:17:58.130 --> 00:17:59.790
He's flat-lined!

00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:01.790
Then resuscitate him, you idiot!

00:18:04.670 --> 00:18:06.920
Well? He still isn't moving!

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:35.880
You don't want him dead, do you?

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:37.960
Just let this end for today.

00:18:39.830 --> 00:18:43.920
Captain Rochina, perhaps
he really doesn't know where it is.

00:18:43.920 --> 00:18:48.790
No, he's resisting us. I know he's hiding something.

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:00.630
I hear his heart stopped once.

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:04.500
Three days he's had to take that torture
and he still won't talk.

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:06.960
Stubborn SOB, isn't he?

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:09.830
I give him two, three days more, tops.

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:12.170
Nobody can stand up to Captain Rochina.

00:19:23.540 --> 00:19:25.290
Looks like it didn't lock down.

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:26.710
Looks closed to me.

00:19:27.210 --> 00:19:29.750
Wonder what's wrong? I'll check it out.

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:40.830
Funny, I don't see anything...

00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:16.460
Who's responsible?

00:20:16.830 --> 00:20:18.960
Sir! I am, Sir.

00:20:20.250 --> 00:20:22.290
Get everyone on this! Move it!

00:20:22.290 --> 00:20:23.750
I want the entire base locked down now!

00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:24.250
Sir!

00:21:34.580 --> 00:21:35.670
There he is!

00:21:48.750 --> 00:21:50.960
Captain! Chirico's escaped!

00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:51.670
What?

00:21:51.670 --> 00:21:53.750
He just stole a fighter!

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:56.420
Damn you, Chirico...

00:21:56.420 --> 00:21:58.000
Do we go after him?

00:21:58.000 --> 00:21:59.670
Captain, what are your orders?

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:02.080
Stop, there's no reason to panic.

00:22:02.630 --> 00:22:07.380
Dr. Fuusen implanted a tracking beacon into his body.

00:22:09.790 --> 00:22:14.040
Activate all ground and satellite-based
surveillance systems!

00:22:26.040 --> 00:22:28.960
He knows... He knows!

00:22:34.460 --> 00:22:40.040
That day, the accursed war
which had so disrupted my destiny ended.

00:22:40.710 --> 00:22:42.920
But its end was ultimately meaningless for me.

00:22:42.920 --> 00:22:47.080
The moment I saw her, my own private war had begun.

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:50.420
A war for which there would be no end.

00:22:54.630 --> 00:22:56.000
NEXT EPISODE

00:22:57.790 --> 00:23:02.920
After escaping Rochina's clutches,
Chirico once more descends into Hell.

00:23:02.920 --> 00:23:05.670
In the aftermath of destruction
dwells violence and desire...

00:23:05.670 --> 00:23:08.500
in a new Sodom born of the Hundred Years War.

00:23:08.790 --> 00:23:11.630
Evil and treachery, corruption and confusion.

00:23:11.630 --> 00:23:14.000
All ground together as though
poured from the same cement mixer.

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:16.670
Melkia's very own Gomorrah.

00:23:17.630 --> 00:23:19.420
Next time, "Uoodo".

00:23:19.420 --> 00:23:22.330
Next week, Chirico takes you with him into Hell.

00:23:20.130 --> 00:23:24.630
NEXT EPISODE UOODO

00:23:42.880 --> 00:23:46.330
Whenever I'm feeling lonely

00:23:46.330 --> 00:23:49.880
Whenever I'm feeling sad

00:23:49.880 --> 00:23:56.250
I can always see you floating in my mind

00:23:56.750 --> 00:24:00.290
Whenever I'm alone

00:24:00.290 --> 00:24:03.710
Whenever I long for you

00:24:03.710 --> 00:24:09.960
I can always feel you inside my heart

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:13.460
No matter how far apart we may go

00:24:13.460 --> 00:24:16.880
No matter if my path should part from yours

00:24:17.040 --> 00:24:23.380
The memories of you seem to shine inside my heart...

00:24:23.750 --> 00:24:29.710
Brighter than any other light...
